---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@data/site";
import { leadershipNetwork, leadershipResponsibilities } from "@data/research";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Leadership"
  description="SCSDA's early platform construction is presented through formal founding leadership, research-centre development, collaboration, and applied project delivery."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Founding Leadership</p>
        <h2>Founding leadership and platform development.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section-copy">
        <p>
          SCSDA's early platform-construction period was initiated and led by
          Dr Daguang Han. The work covered institutional planning,
          research-centre development, international academic links, enterprise
          engagement, and the delivery of applied research projects. This page
          presents leadership as an institutional function: setting research
          directions, building a centre structure, coordinating expert
          participation, developing partner-facing projects, and communicating
          applied research outputs through public channels.
        </p>
        <p>
          During this period, Dr Han served as Founding Dean of the Academy,
          named as its designated head in the Liangjiang New Area government
          approval of March 2019, and acted as the founding executive lead for
          the early research platform. The wider structure also involved expert
          advisers, centre-level academic and technical leads, project
          collaborators, and enterprise-facing partners connected to SCSDA's
          smart city, digital construction, sensing, and sustainable
          development agenda.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Academy's cross-border work has also been carried at governance
          level rather than only at project level: Dr Han serves as
          Vice-President of the International Innovation Cooperation Center
          (ICIC), a body chaired by Professor Michael Kraft of KU Leuven. That
          vantage informs how SCSDA structures its own partnerships &mdash;
          every joint centre rests on a dated signed agreement, because an
          arrangement that has to survive staff changes on both sides cannot
          rest on personal contact alone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell highlight-grid">
      <article class="case-card">
        <img
          src="/images/sensor-calibration-equipment.jpg"
          alt="Precision sensor development and calibration equipment in an Academy laboratory"
          width="1080"
          height="720"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div class="case-body">
          <span class="category">Working style</span>
          <h3>Leadership close to the laboratory</h3>
          <p>Platform leadership at SCSDA stays close to the technical work: reviewing experimental setups and instrumentation, and connecting research groups with the questions their methods can answer.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Leadership Structure</p>
        <h2>Founder, expert committee, research centres, and project collaboration.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        The Academy's platform was developed through founding leadership,
        expert engagement, research-centre coordination, project delivery, and
        collaboration with academic and enterprise partners. This structure is
        important because it shows how SCSDA moved from an institutional idea
        into a working applied research platform with recognisable roles,
        themes, centres, and public outputs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell theme-grid">
      {leadershipNetwork.map((item) => (
        <article class="theme-card">
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Founding Leadership Scope</p>
        <h2>Strategic, academic, and industry-facing responsibilities.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Founding leadership is presented as platform-building work: agenda
        setting, centre formation, partner development, project formation,
        expert engagement, institutional reporting, and public communication.
        These responsibilities describe the practical work behind creating a
        research academy: translating a technical strategy into centres,
        projects, people, partnerships, and outputs that can be reviewed by
        academic and industry audiences.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell theme-grid">
      {leadershipResponsibilities.map((item) => (
        <article class="theme-card">
          <h3>{item.title}</h3>
          <p>{item.text}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell article narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">External References</p>
      <h2>Selected public reference links.</h2>
      <p>
        Selected public reference links are provided only for source
        transparency where founding leadership is discussed.
      </p>
      <div class="profile-links">
        {site.profiles.map((profile) => (
          <a href={profile.href} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">{profile.label}</a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
